.TH "NIX\-BUILDS.TOML" "5" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
nix\-builds.toml \- catalog configuration for Nix expression builds
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]nix\-builds.toml\f[R] file declares external catalogs that are
made available to Nix expression builds within a Flox environment.
It lives at \f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.toml\f[R] alongside the environment
manifest.
.SH DESCRIPTION
When a Flox environment uses Nix expression builds (packages defined as
\f[CR].nix\f[R] files under \f[CR].flox/pkgs/\f[R]), those expressions
can depend on packages provided by external catalogs.
The \f[CR]nix\-builds.toml\f[R] file declares which catalogs are
available and where they come from.
.PP
Running \f[CR]flox build update\-catalogs\f[R] resolves every catalog
entry and writes the pinned result to \f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.lock\f[R].
Both files should be committed to version control.
.SS \f[CR]version\f[R]
Required.
The configuration format version.
Currently the only supported value is \f[CR]1\f[R].
.IP
.EX
version = 1
.EE
.SS \f[CR][catalogs.<name>]\f[R]
Each section under \f[CR]catalogs\f[R] declares a single catalog.
The \f[CR]<name>\f[R] becomes the key used to reference the catalog in
Nix expressions: a package \f[CR]foo\f[R] in catalog
\f[CR]mycatalog\f[R] is accessed as \f[CR]catalogs.mycatalog.foo\f[R].
.PP
A catalog can be specified in one of three forms.
.SS Structured Nix source type
Provide a \f[CR]type\f[R] field naming a Nix source type together with
additional fields appropriate to that type:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][catalogs.mycatalog]\f[R]
type = \(dqgit\(dq
url = \(dqhttps://github.com/org/repo\(dq
ref = \(dqmain\(dq
.EE
.PP
The supported types and their fields are documented in the \f[B]Nix
manual under \f[BI]Source
types\f[B]\f[R] <\f[I]https://nix.dev/manual/nix/latest/language/builtins.html#source\-types\f[R]>.
.SS URL string
As a shorthand for the structured form, provide a single \f[CR]url\f[R]
field containing a Nix source reference:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][catalogs.mycatalog]\f[R]
url = \(dqgit+https://github.com/org/repo\(dq
.EE
.PP
The URL follows Nix source reference syntax and may include query
parameters such as \f[CR]?ref=<branch>\f[R] or \f[CR]?rev=<commit>\f[R].
.SS FloxHub catalog
Set \f[CR]type\f[R] to \f[CR]\(dqfloxhub\(dq\f[R] to pull packages from
a catalog published on FloxHub:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][catalogs.mycatalog]\f[R]
type = \(dqfloxhub\(dq
.EE
.PP
The catalog name must match a catalog identifier registered on FloxHub.
.SS Lockfile
Running \f[CR]flox build update\-catalogs\f[R] produces
\f[CR].flox/nix\-builds.lock\f[R], a JSON file that pins every catalog
to a specific resolved state.
The lockfile is consumed at build time; it must be present and up to
date before running \f[CR]flox build\f[R] on packages that reference
catalogs.
.SS Using catalogs in Nix expressions
Nix expressions under \f[CR].flox/pkgs/\f[R] receive a
\f[CR]catalogs\f[R] argument.
Each catalog declared in \f[CR]nix\-builds.toml\f[R] appears as an
attribute set keyed by \f[CR]<name>\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# .flox/pkgs/hello.nix\f[R]
{ catalogs }:
catalogs.mycatalog.some\-package
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Declare a Git catalog
.IP
.EX
version = 1

\f[B][catalogs.mylib]\f[R]
url = \(dqgit+https://github.com/org/mylib\(dq
.EE
.SS Declare a catalog with a pinned branch
.IP
.EX
version = 1

\f[B][catalogs.mylib]\f[R]
type = \(dqgit\(dq
url = \(dqhttps://github.com/org/mylib\(dq
ref = \(dqrelease\-2.0\(dq
.EE
.SS Declare a FloxHub catalog
.IP
.EX
version = 1

\f[B][catalogs.myorg]\f[R]
type = \(dqfloxhub\(dq
.EE
.SS Use a catalog in a package expression
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# .flox/pkgs/app.nix\f[R]
{ catalogs }:
catalogs.myorg.build\-tool
.EE
